	"rows": [
		{
			"id": "e-DUQph2c9GclUDV2",
			"description": "Lascannon",
			"local_notes": "Needs a tripod or vehicle pit mount (ST 12M): an unmounted human cannot brace it, though Astartes ST lets a Space Marine fire it standing (treat as braced at ST 12 rather than mounted, GM's call). Draws from a dedicated power cell (see Lascannon Power Cell); swapping cells takes the 5-turn reload noted in shots.\n\nLore: The definitive Imperial anti-tank weapon: Guard heavy weapons squads, Space Marine Devastators and Predator/Rhino/Razorback sponsons and turrets all mount it, and Black Library fiction (Gaunt's Ghosts, Horus Heresy novels) consistently has a well-placed lascannon shot cripple or kill a battle tank, and treats it as one of the few man-portable weapons that can bring down a Terminator or walker.\n\nDesign: Damage is the fixed anchor from framework.md: 8dx4(5) burn (\"kills tanks and Terminators\"). Checked against the vehicle AV table: average 112 burn through an armor divisor of 5 gives an effective DR of 10 (AV10) to 50 (AV14). Even a worst-case minimum roll (8 dice all at 1, x4 = 32) clears every effective DR on the table, so the lascannon reliably beats AV10 through AV14 (DR50-250) with the anchor's divisor doing almost all the work; only the same DR80 that stops most other man-portable weapons (Astartes power armor, Tactical Dreadnought DR80) is trivial for it, matching \"kills tanks and Terminators\" without exception. Acc, range, RoF, shots, Bulk and Rcl are not anchored by framework.md, so they're built from first principles: RoF 1 and Rcl 1 because a beam weapon has no recoil and the capacitor cycle time is the limiting factor; Acc 14 and a long 1500/4500 range because the weapon's entire battlefield role is precision fire on distant armor, which demands better optics than a lasgun (Acc 10); Bulk -8 and ST 12M because the weapon and its cooling housing are backpack-sized and unwieldy without a brace. Cost and LC follow \"military-issue heavy weapons\" (LC2) and are priced well above a lasgun to reflect scarcity of the long-barrel focusing crystal.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
