		{
			"id": "e5-8S43cAboPwdG4j",
			"description": "Lascannon Power Cell",
			"local_notes": "Good for 5 shots per the lascannon's shots rating. A spent cell must be sent back to an armoury or Tech-Priest for recharging; it isn't a field-rechargeable pack like a lasgun's.\n\nLore: Described in Guard logistics fiction as a heavy, closely-guarded item; a heavy weapons team is only as good as its ammo carrier's supply of charged cells.\n\nDesign: Weight and cost scaled up from a lasgun power pack (a small, cheap, common item) by roughly the same ratio as the lascannon's damage output over a lasgun's, since it stores far more energy in a denser, more dangerous cell. No anchor fixes this number; it exists to make ammunition resupply a logistics concern in play.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum",
				"Adeptus Astartes",
				"Ammunition"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "2",
			"base_value": "2000",
			"base_weight": "15 lb",
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "e30vWMZlseagncPa7",
			"description": "Heavy Weapon Tripod",
			"local_notes": "Required to fire a mounted-only (M) heavy weapon without an Astartes-grade ST score. Setup/breakdown takes about a minute (Fast-Draw or GM discretion can shorten this).\n\nLore: Guard heavy weapons squads are built around a two- or three-man team - gunner, loader, and often an ammo carrier - who move the tripod between firing positions, a staple of Astra Militarum fiction from Gaunt's Ghosts onward.\n\nDesign: Not anchored; a generic piece of gear so lascannon, multi-laser, autocannon and mortar entries can all reference the same mount rather than each inventing one. Cost and weight are a plausible generic tripod, not derived from any weapon-specific figure.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum",
				"Gear"
			],
			"tech_level": "8",
			"legality_class": "3",
			"base_value": "300",
			"base_weight": "20 lb",
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "e4n2vn8WSqQOwmFOy",
			"description": "Multi-laser, Tripod-Mounted",
			"local_notes": "More commonly seen as a Sentinel or Rhino turret weapon than carried into the field; this is the static defensive-emplacement or bunker version issued to line regiments guarding a position.\n\nLore: Multi-lasers are the standard secondary and light-vehicle turret weapon across the Astra Militarum (Sentinels, Chimeras, Rhinos); fiction and background consistently treat them as good infantry-shredders that struggle to hurt anything with real armour plate.\n\nDesign: No framework anchor covers the multi-laser, so it's built by extrapolating from the lasgun anchor (4d burn) rather than any catalogue \"laser cannon\" entry: a multi-laser is several linked lasgun-grade emitters cycling fast, so damage per shot only steps up a little (5d, roughly one step above the lasgun the way a hellgun steps up for penetration instead) while RoF 3 represents the linked barrels. Checked against the vehicle AV table: even a maximum roll (5d = 30) never reaches the AV10/DR50 effective threshold, so the multi-laser cannot reliably beat any vehicle on that table - it has no armor divisor to help it, unlike the lascannon or krak missile. This matches the fiction, where multi-laser-armed Sentinels and Rhinos support infantry and duel light, often open-topped raiders and buggies (DR well under the AV10 line) rather than trade blows with tanks. Acc, range and Bulk sit between the lasgun and lascannon since the weapon is a scaled-up rifle on a mount, not a dedicated tank-killer.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "2",
