		{
			"id": "eGuN7Vv92kT-L1H3J",
			"description": "Autocannon",
			"local_notes": "Weight includes the tripod mount; a Heavy Weapons Squad crews it as gunner plus loader. The Predator battle tank's turret gun is the same weapon on a stabilised vehicle mount.\n\nLore: The autocannon is the Guard heavy weapons squad's and the Predator tank's main anti-light-vehicle gun throughout the fiction: reliably described tearing through Ork trukks, light xenos raiders and Sentinel-class walkers, denting Rhinos and Chimeras, and bouncing or only chipping a Leman Russ or Land Raider's frontal glacis.\n\nDesign: Not covered by a framework anchor, so it's built as a solid-projectile \"stub\" weapon per the TL table (autogun/stubber bracket, scaled to artillery-grade tolerances) rather than borrowed from any GURPS catalogue cannon: a single heavy AP penetrator per round gives pi++ (full wound multiplier, no follow-up), with a light armor divisor (2) for the hardened long-rod core, and a real cannon's low-teens RoF is dialed back to RoF 3 to keep it a burst weapon rather than a chain-gun (that's the assault cannon's niche). Checked shot-by-shot against the vehicle AV table using the average (6dx2 = 42) and the full 6-36 spread of 6d before doubling: it clears AV10 (DR50, eff. DR25) on the large majority of rolls - reliably beats; splits close to even against AV11 (DR80, eff. DR40, needs 6d > 20 against a mean of 21) - Rhino sides, matching \"dents a Rhino\"; only the top of the 6d range clears AV12 (DR120, eff. DR60, needs 6d > 30) - rarely beats a Chimera's front; and it mathematically cannot clear AV13 or AV14 (needs 6d > 45, impossible on 6d) - cannot beat a Leman Russ or Land Raider's armour, matching every source that has autocannon fire shrug off a main battle tank's frontal plate.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "8",
			"legality_class": "2",
