		{
			"id": "eAhzkgNzbb4S-gf29",
			"description": "Missile Launcher",
			"local_notes": "Shoulder-fired, one missile loaded at a time; the gunner (or a loader) carries spares separately (see the missile entries below). Flakk missiles trade blast for a proximity fuze and are wasted against ground targets.\n\nLore: The Guard's man-portable answer to armour and aircraft when a lascannon isn't to hand: fiction repeatedly has missile teams crack light and medium vehicles and occasionally cripple a Leman Russ, while frag loads are the squad's answer to entrenched infantry and light structures.\n\nDesign: No single framework anchor, so each warhead is derived separately. Krak: built as a one-shot, disposable shaped charge, using the same armor-divisor family as the lascannon's beam (5) rather than a catalogue HEAT rocket, but with far fewer raw dice (6dx2, avg. 42) since it's a single expendable warhead, not a capacitor weapon - the framework's own description of it as \"lascannon-lite vs. armour.\" Checked against the AV table: it reliably beats AV10 (DR50, eff. DR10) through AV12 (DR120, eff. DR24, needs only 6d > 12 against a mean of 21); splits roughly even against AV13 (DR180, eff. DR36, needs 6d > 18); and only the top of the 6d range clears AV14 (DR250, eff. DR50, needs 6d > 25) - so it can reliably wreck Chimeras and Rhinos, sometimes hurts a Leman Russ, and only rarely alone cracks a Land Raider, which is why the fiction has missile teams engage such targets in numbers rather than solo. Frag: scaled from the B414 fragmentation rules as a \"big frag grenade\" per the framework's own description - roughly double the blast and fragmentation dice of a standard hand grenade (3d[3d]) to reflect a much larger warhead, giving 6d cr ex [6d]; it has no armor divisor and is not intended to threaten anything on the vehicle AV table, only infantry and light cover. Flakk: the frag warhead's dice with a proximity fuze instead of impact/frag optimisation, at one die less since more of the casing goes into the fuze and less into the frag liner; it is not rated against ground DR at all. Acc/range/RoF/Bulk are shared across usages since they describe the launcher, not the warhead, and are built as a shoulder-fired tube (lower ST and Bulk penalty than the tripod weapons above, since one Guardsman carries and fires it solo).",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
