		{
			"id": "eM4dDI14OtE0RKYeG",
			"description": "Assault Cannon (Soulreaper Pattern)",
			"local_notes": "Arm- or hip-socket mounted on Terminator armour, or carried and fired one-handed by an Astartes on a stabilising harness; ST 15 assumes Astartes-grade strength rather than a tripod.\n\nLore: Devastator squads and Terminators use the multi-barrelled assault cannon (also fielded by Chaos as the Soulreaper cannon) as a close-to-mid-range storm of solid shot for shredding infantry, light vehicles and swarms; it is fired solid rounds rather than bolts, which is why it sits outside the bolt-weapon family, and fiction almost always pairs it with a melee specialist (power fist, thunder hammer) on the same Terminator rather than relying on it against tanks.\n\nDesign: No framework anchor, so it's built parallel to the heavy bolter anchor (8d(2) pi+, follow-up 4d cr ex) rather than copied from it: the assault cannon fires solid rotary-autocannon-style rounds with no explosive follow-up, so it drops the follow-up term and scales the base damage down one step (5d instead of 8d) in exchange for a much higher RoF (10 vs. the heavy bolter's typical squad-support RoF), matching its fluff role as a horde-clearing hail of fire rather than a hard-hitting single line of shots. Checked against the vehicle AV table: even at RoF 10, no single round (max 5d(2) = 30, eff. DR halved) reliably clears AV10's effective DR25, so it cannot reliably beat any vehicle on the table - consistent with Astartes fiction, where the assault cannon is a horde/infantry weapon and its wielder relies on a paired melee weapon (power fist, thunder hammer) or a squadmate's lascannon/missile launcher against real armour. LC1 follows the framework's Astartes-gear bracket (alongside bolters and plasma) rather than the Guard's LC2 heavy-weapon bracket.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
