		{
			"id": "epJ5arNy0SkduUU6Y",
			"description": "Mortar",
			"local_notes": "Baseplate, bipod and tube break down for a three-man crew to carry; minimum range reflects the bomb's arming distance, not a targeting limit. Uses the indirect-fire rules under Artillery, not a direct line of sight.\n\nLore: The mortar is the Guard's simplest and most ubiquitous indirect-fire support weapon, issued down to platoon level in Guard fiction for exactly the reason real-world mortars are: cheap, rugged, easy to manufacture on almost any forge world, and effective against dug-in infantry and soft targets beyond line of sight.\n\nDesign: No framework anchor, so it's placed at the bottom of the TL table deliberately - mortar tube technology is older and simpler than lasguns, stubbers or rockets, which is exactly why every regiment from a hive world to a feral-world levy can field one. Damage is built the same way as the missile launcher's frag warhead (B414 fragmentation, \"big frag grenade\" scaling) but roughly doubled again, since a mortar bomb is not weight-constrained by a rocket motor and can devote more of its mass to filler and casing, giving 6dx2 cr ex [6d]. It carries no armor divisor and is not intended to be checked against the vehicle AV table at all - its role in the fiction is area denial and infantry suppression, not armour-killing, so unlike the autocannon, krak missile or lascannon above it has no reliably/ sometimes/cannot-beat line against AV10-14.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "6",
			"legality_class": "2",
			"base_value": "2000",
			"base_weight": "40 lb",
